# =============================================================================
# luispollon.com — environment
#
# Copy to .env.local for development; set the same keys in the Vercel project
# for preview and production.
#
# Every variable here is OPTIONAL. Left empty, the corresponding script is
# never rendered — the site builds, runs and deploys with this file untouched
# and ships zero third-party JavaScript. That is the intended default, not a
# broken state: add an ID only when there is a question you actually want it
# to answer.
# =============================================================================

# --- Google Analytics 4 ------------------------------------------------------
# Measurement ID from the GA4 data stream (Admin → Data streams → Web).
# Writes to the reader's device, so it loads only after consent is granted.
# Consent Mode v2 runs with the ad signals denied permanently — this site runs
# no advertising and has nothing to grant them for.
# Format: G-XXXXXXXXXX
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID=

# --- Microsoft Clarity -------------------------------------------------------
# Project ID from clarity.microsoft.com (Settings → Overview → Project ID).
# Heatmaps and session replay. Also device storage, also consent-gated.
# Format: 10-character alphanumeric string
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLARITY_ID=

# --- Vercel Analytics --------------------------------------------------------
# No variable. The platform injects the endpoint at deploy time, and the script
# is cookieless — nothing is stored on or read from the device, so it is not
# consent-gated and runs on every page view. Enable or disable it in the Vercel
# project dashboard (Analytics tab), not here.
